hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1579","Harun bin Ishaq told us, Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Amara bin Al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace, when he said “Allahu Akbar” during prayer, he remained silent between saying “Allahu Akbar” and reading, so I said to him: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you. Did you see your silence between saying “Allahu Akbar”? And reading, tell me what it is? He said: “I say: Oh God, distance me from my sin as you distanced between the East and the West. Oh God, save me from my sins like a white garment.” From filth, O God, wash me from my sins with ice, water, and hail.”"
